{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 \fswiss Helvetica;}{\f1 \fmodern Courier;}}
{\colortbl;\red255\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;}
\widowctrl\hyphauto

{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Turns the REAPER transport state into a parameter: 1 while playing or recording, 0 otherwise (stopped or paused). Use it as a source for Parameter Modulation / Link from FX parameter, so another plugin parameter can follow play/stop (e.g. switch an effect on only during playback, or reset something on start). Audio and MIDI are not touched.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 PARAMETERS Play State [Readout] Output: 1 = playing or recording, 0 = stopped / paused. Do not edit by hand.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 NOTE: the track must be processed while the transport is stopped for the 0 to be reported (enable "Run FX when stopped" in REAPER's FX / track settings).\par}
}

